It also depends on whether the CC is a valid initial pair. If it isn't, and=
=20
the stress is on the penult, you get a word like "baldakino" (which is some=
=20
cloth I never heard of before) or "kardamomo".

If the stress is on the first syllable, it breaks apart as CVCCV CV CV,=20
regardless of whether CC is a valid initial. If the stress is on the second=
,=20
you get CVCCVCV CV or CV CCVCV CV, depending on whether CC is a valid initi=
al.

I came up with "lokrataigo" as an example. "l=C3=B3krataigo" is "lokra tai =
go"=20
(which is part of the grammatical utterance "lokra tai go ti gi ta").=20
"lokrat=C3=A1igo" is "lo krataigo". So you can say "lokra tai go lo krataig=
o gi lo=20
fagjesyspa".

